# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.wasm
# root-level stray build artifact (go build -o wasm ./cmd/wasm); the bare
# pattern used to shadow the cmd/wasm SOURCE dir and forced -f adds
/wasm
# same class (go build ./tools/govulncheck-filter drops the binary at the root):
# root-anchored so it cannot shadow the tracked tools/govulncheck-filter SOURCE
# dir. Left untracked in the driver-pin worktree since 2026-08-15, and mission
# iterations 213/214/215 each had to note and route around it at Gate 0.
/govulncheck-filter

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Built binaries
/ailang
bin/ailang
/bin
/build-snapshot

# MCP snapshot output — generated by `make snapshot`, rebuilt every release.
# Cloud Run images bake this in at build time; local dev/CI regenerates.
build/snapshot/

# Generated Go code from compiler (root-level only, not internal/gen/)
/gen/

# CI/CD generated files
examples_report.json
examples_status.md
coverage.txt

# Eval harness runtime artifacts
benchmark/solution*.ail
data/
output/
.eval_workspace/
# Benchmark side-effect files written to repo root by FS-effecting benchmarks
# (log_file_analyzer writes app.log, config_file_parser writes app_config.json, etc.)
# These leak from temp dirs when an agent's working directory resolves to repo root.
/app.log
/app_config.json
/output.txt
/users.csv
/users.json
/widget_price.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Agent protocol runtime state (like .git/)
.ailang/
# ...EXCEPT the sprint state files, which are a pipeline ARTIFACT, not runtime
# scratch. sprint-planner declares `.ailang/state/sprints/*.json` in its
# artifact_patterns and sprint-executor REFUSES to start without the matching
# file — so ignoring them makes the handoff between those two agents impossible
# to complete.
#
# Measured 2026-09-14: sprint-planner produced a 178-line plan, it merged, and
# sprint-executor then stopped with "Execution is blocked by the mandatory
# sprint-executor gate: .ailang/state/sprints/sprint_M-OPENROUTER-EU-ROUTING.json
# is missing." The planner had nothing to commit it WITH; `git add` skipped it
# in silence. Older sprint JSONs are in the repo only because they were tracked
# before this rule, and gitignore does not apply to already-tracked files —
# which is exactly why the gap was invisible.
#
# Git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, so each level
# is re-admitted in turn. Everything else under .ailang/ stays ignored.
# The exceptions are anchored to the repo root on purpose: an unanchored
# `!.ailang/` re-admits every nested `.ailang/cache` the compiler drops next
# to a source file (examples/**/.ailang showed as untracked for months).
!/.ailang/
/.ailang/*
!/.ailang/state/
/.ailang/state/*
!/.ailang/state/sprints/
!/.ailang/state/sprints/*.json
# ...and the simplicity-metrics snapshots (M-V1-SIMPLIFY-S1): the weekly audit
# diffs against the last banked one, so they must travel with the repo.
!/.ailang/state/simplicity/
!/.ailang/state/simplicity/*.json
/ui/node_modules
internal/executor/opencode/plugins/node_modules
internal/executor/opencode/plugins/coverage

# Temporary data
temp_data/

# Eval raw run results (regeneratable; only baselines/ and performance_tables/ are committed)
eval_results/
!eval_results/baselines/
!eval_results/performance_tables/
ui/.env.local
code-harness-skills/
# Stray compiled binary (build output lands in repo root)
/registry-validator
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/
# Per-developer Claude Code overrides. settings.json is shared (project-wide
# permission allowlist + hooks); settings.local.json is the personal-overrides
# slot every developer keeps locally.
.claude/settings.local.json

# sim_stub example: binary is regenerated by `make test` inside examples/sim_stub/
# (see make test-sim-stub / .github/workflows/test-game-codegen.yml). The copy
# in-tree was removed in M4 of M-SUPPLY-CHAIN-HARDENING.
/examples/sim_stub/sim_stub
/examples/sim_stub/sim_stub_release
.DS_Store
smoke-motoko
/tmp
design_docs/research/*.pdf

# Machine-local pi state (per-session agent-name marker; never versioned)
.ailang_voice

# Harness scratch dirs. scripts/test_fmt_check.sh, scripts/test_shellcheck_autopush.sh and
# scripts/hooks/test_push_dev_on_stop.sh mktemp INSIDE the repo (deliberately — a /tmp-rooted
# checkout makes CWD-relative path tests fail for the location rather than the code). Their
# EXIT traps clean up; these two lines cover the SIGKILL/crash case only.
.tmp-fmt-check.*
.tmp-iter327.*

# Build/scratch outputs at the root (M-V1-SIMPLIFY-S1 M5)
/gen/
/.eval_workspace/
